   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Mass action law"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "At a given temperature the product of electron and hole concentrations is fixed: $n p = n_i^2$. In n-type, $n \\approx N_D$ and $p = n_i^2/N_D$, a very small number. In p-type, $p \\approx N_A$ and $n = n_i^2/N_A$. Adding majority carriers increases recombination, so the minority carriers become fewer than in the pure crystal."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "n-type: n ≈ N_D, p = nᵢ²/N_D"
    },
    {
     "en": "p-type: p ≈ N_A, n = nᵢ²/N_A"
    },
    {
     "en": "Donor level just below CB; acceptor level just above VB"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "The mass action law says n times p equals n i squared. So in n-type the holes become very few, and in p-type the electrons become very few.",
